                <pb facs="0090" n="2" sameAs="frus:frus1933v05/pg2"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">824.512/49: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Minister in Bolivia</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Feely</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1932-09-22T17:00:00-04:00">September 22, 1932—5
                        p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>36. Your 85, September 19, 2 p.m. Judging from information received, Department
                    doubts whether article 3 or any part of our treaty with Bolivia is violated by
                    the proposed bill. If bill becomes law and you are still of the opinion that
                    stipulations of the treaty are involved, please cable further details and your
                    reasons therefor.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Stimson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
